---Create a plugin that a project publishes
---
---Requires project#manage on owner_project_id. Any other caller gets 404, as for a project that does not exist. owner_project_id must name a native Entire project; a mirrored project is refused with owner_project_not_native. The plugin starts unlisted. A project owns at most 100 plugins; more is refused with plugin_limit_reached. Entire sets listed and repo_create_daily_limit; the plugin's owner reads them. Core fetches a jwks_url once before saving it. logo_url must name an image the caller uploaded with an entire.com session to PUT /api/v1/plugin-images on the web app origin; a replace may also keep the plugin's current logo. A save that sets a new upload publishes it, and a replace deletes the uploaded logo it replaced. An expired upload is refused with logo_upload_expired. A create whose logo is refused still creates the plugin, without a published logo.
---
---`POST /api/v1/plugin-registrations`
---@param input entire.plugins.CreatePluginRegistrationRequest
---@return entire.plugins.PluginRegistration? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
